% Terms are rational trees (Prolog II/III): unification has no occurs check,
% and a cyclic term is a legitimate value, printed as an equation.
omega(X) :- { X = f(X) }.
stream(S) :- { S = cons(1, S) }.
same(X, X).

?- omega(X).
?- omega(X), { X = f(f(X)) }.
?- omega(X), omega(Y), same(X, Y).
?- stream(S).
?- { X = g(Y, Y), Y = h(X) }.
?- { X = f(X, a) }, { X = f(X, b) }.
